{{!-- /admin/moos/app/ : MOOS on the web (Ian, 2026-11-25: "When you open
     up /admin, I want a toggle on the bottom right that says 'Try MOOS'...
     every board needs to work on web"). The contract is MOCA
     website/moos/WEB.md; this page is its piece B.

     A standalone document, like the journal readers, so it does not extend
     default.hbs: MOOS is a full-screen app with its own rail and its own
     stylesheet, and the site's header, footer, screen.css and site bundle
     would sit on top of it and restyle its controls.

     What loads, in order:
       1. js/moos-web-config.js sets window.MOOS_WEB from the theme settings
          on its data attributes (the CSP allows no inline script).
       2. moos-app-head: fonts, MOOS's stylesheet, d3 and topojson.
       3. js/error-beacon.js, so MOOS's errors and CSP refusals reach
          mo-errors like the rest of the site's.
       4. js/admin-auth.js: window.MOAuth, the staff bearer. It reads the
          mo-trusted-hosts meta below once, as it loads.
       5. moos-app-body: assets/moos/web.js (the web adapter, piece C), then
          MOOS's markup, its core module and its parts.
       6. The "Try MOOS" switch, on.
     Both moos-app-* partials and everything in assets/moos/ are GENERATED
     by scripts/build-moos.mjs from the MOCA. Re-run it when MOOS changes.

     Staff only, the way the other admin pages gate: the template shows MOOS
     to a signed-in member, and mo-admin's /moos/web/* routes answer Ghost
     staff and nobody else. A signed-out visitor gets the admin pages'
     "Staff only" panel.

     CSP: the site's policy narrowed to what MOOS uses. Scripts from this
     site and three pinned jsDelivr packages (d3, topojson, and xlsx when a
     workbook is saved; build-moos.mjs fails if MOOS uses one not listed in
     script-src); data from mo-admin, mo-email, the podcast feed and
     mo-errors. A new worker for MOOS goes in connect-src here and in
     moos-web-config.js's data attributes, and in mo-trusted-hosts too if it
     takes the staff bearer.

     Leave /admin/moos/ (custom-admin-moos.hbs, the desktop pairing page)
     alone: it is a different page. --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3@7.9.0/ https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/topojson@3.0.2/ https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/xlsx@0.18.5/; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; connect-src 'self' https://mo-admin.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-email.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-podcast-feed.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-errors.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev; frame-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests" />
  <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <title>MOOS | MO Admin</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Internal Mere Orthodoxy staff tool." />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f3f2" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#24201e" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
  {{!-- MOAuth.fetch attaches the staff bearer only to these hosts: exactly
       the two workers that take it, mo-admin and mo-email. MOOS reaches the
       podcast feed and this site with a plain fetch (bridge.js, auth: false),
       so neither is here. Narrower than default.hbs's list on purpose. --}}
  <meta name="mo-trusted-hosts" content="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}|https://mo-email.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/jpeg" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
  {{#if @member}}
  <script src="{{asset "js/moos-web-config.js"}}" data-admin="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}" data-email="https://mo-email.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" data-podcast="{{#if @custom.podcast_feed_url}}{{@custom.podcast_feed_url}}{{else}}https://mo-podcast-feed.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev{{/if}}"></script>
  {{> "moos-app-head"}}
  {{else}}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IM+Fell+Great+Primer:ital@0;1&family=Source+Serif+Pro:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400;1,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="{{asset "built/screen.min.css"}}" />
  {{/if}}
</head>
<body class="moos-web"
      {{#if @member}}data-member-email="{{@member.email}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.admin_worker_url}}data-admin-worker-url="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      data-error-worker-url="{{#if @custom.error_worker_url}}{{@custom.error_worker_url}}{{else}}https://mo-errors.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev{{/if}}">
  <script src="{{asset "js/error-beacon.js"}}"></script>
  <script src="{{asset "js/admin-auth.js"}}"></script>
  {{#if @member}}
    {{> "moos-app-body"}}
    {{> "moos-switch" app=true}}
  {{else}}
    <main class="admin-page">
      {{> "admin-denied"}}
    </main>
  {{/if}}
</body>
</html>
